(7339995, 1146719, 100831, '<td valign="top">Unique for Ubique... I hope he likes this one as much as I do:) bump.</td>', 'Unique for Ubique... I hope he likes this one as much as I do:) bump.', '2015-04-09 10:01:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340004, 1146704, 173844, '<td valign="top"><strike></strike></td>', '', '2015-04-09 10:09:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340023, 1146528, 108069, '<td valign="top">Very nicely framed, they against the light field of cement, some texture and lines, and impressive-in-their-unimpressiveness geometric structures. Buttery smooth.</td>', 'Very nicely framed, they against the light field of cement, some texture and lines, and impressive-in-their-unimpressiveness geometric structures. Buttery smooth.', '2015-04-09 12:14:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340024, 1146587, 108069, '<td valign="top">Nicely found. Great tones and processing. Really like how this is framed. A comforting, structural piece of art.</td>', 'Nicely found. Great tones and processing. Really like how this is framed. A comforting, structural piece of art.', '2015-04-09 12:15:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340025, 1146564, 108069, '<td valign="top">Great title. Nice tones, very well spotted. This is what happens when you your eyes are open all the time and you''ve got the spirit to just see what happens.</td>', 'Great title. Nice tones, very well spotted. This is what happens when you your eyes are open all the time and you''ve got the spirit to just see what happens.', '2015-04-09 12:18:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340031, 1146473, 30364, '<td valign="top">Awwww, you''ve been peeking at something of mine, and you have thoroughly thrashed me at my own game.  That''s nearly an elephant ... Is it?  It feels like an elephant, although the uncertainty about that question is marvellous to me.  It is, it isn''t, it is, it must be; the real answer doesn''t matter.  This is a beautiful, mystical photograph, perfectly poised on the knife edge between the spiritual and the corporeal.  Had I produced this photograph, I''d have been thrilled and alas, surprised, and very happy.  That a fellow photographer created it in this challenge makes me happier still.  It''s a beautiful thing.  Thank you.</td>', 'Awwww, you''ve been peeking at something of mine, and you have thoroughly thrashed me at my own game.  That''s nearly an elephant ... Is it?  It feels like an elephant, although the uncertainty about that question is marvellous to me.  It is, it isn''t, it is, it must be; the real answer doesn''t matter.  This is a beautiful, mystical photograph, perfectly poised on the knife edge between the spiritual and the corporeal.  Had I produced this photograph, I''d have been thrilled and alas, surprised, and very happy.  That a fellow photographer created it in this challenge makes me happier still.  It''s a beautiful thing.  Thank you.', '2015-04-09 12:46:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340036, 1146564, 30364, '<td valign="top">I cannot resist this kind of photograph.  I use my own side mirrors as a set every time I go out photographing wildlife (where I go you are most unwise to get out of your vehicle).  I love the surreal effect of something in the side mirror; everything looks like Dali was involved.  This one is a great example of the whacky world of side mirror shots.  I''ve yet to figure out how to get an elephant to lie down on the road after I pass by, as has your dog.  But I''ll keep trying after this.  I enjoyed it very much and I thank you.</td>', 'I cannot resist this kind of photograph.  I use my own side mirrors as a set every time I go out photographing wildlife (where I go you are most unwise to get out of your vehicle).  I love the surreal effect of something in the side mirror; everything looks like Dali was involved.  This one is a great example of the whacky world of side mirror shots.  I''ve yet to figure out how to get an elephant to lie down on the road after I pass by, as has your dog.  But I''ll keep trying after this.  I enjoyed it very much and I thank you.', '2015-04-09 12:53:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340043, 1145746, 30364, '<td valign="top">I usually flick past landscapes, but not this one.  The sensual mood that you have created/captured is remarkably beautiful.  Most landscapes are static; they just lie there looking spectacular like a supermodel on a pool lounger.  But yours is dynamic, and that makes all the difference for me; in yours the supermodel is scratching her ... let''s say her ear.  That is, there''s something interesting going on.  The sense of movement, the dance between sand, air and light, is gorgeous.  I think this photograph will go very close to the blue ribbon, and if it does I would not quibble one bit.  It may not be my preferred cup of tea as a genre, but it''s undeniably lovely, stimulating and interesting.  Thank you.</td>', 'I usually flick past landscapes, but not this one.  The sensual mood that you have created/captured is remarkably beautiful.  Most landscapes are static; they just lie there looking spectacular like a supermodel on a pool lounger.  But yours is dynamic, and that makes all the difference for me; in yours the supermodel is scratching her ... let''s say her ear.  That is, there''s something interesting going on.  The sense of movement, the dance between sand, air and light, is gorgeous.  I think this photograph will go very close to the blue ribbon, and if it does I would not quibble one bit.  It may not be my preferred cup of tea as a genre, but it''s undeniably lovely, stimulating and interesting.  Thank you.', '2015-04-09 13:07:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340076, 1145746, 173844, '<td valign="top">A subtle, delicate, howling image.  As the scene recedes in overlapping planes, it''s the second plane that''s in focus, a fine choice that enables the windblown snow to be encompassing rather than fronting.  The lovely, muted palette of green, gray and white exists in fine compositional balance.  The mottled, obscuring background, which actually includes the foreground swirling snow, works as pseudo-bokeh.  One of four personal favorites.</td>', 'A subtle, delicate, howling image.  As the scene recedes in overlapping planes, it''s the second plane that''s in focus, a fine choice that enables the windblown snow to be encompassing rather than fronting.  The lovely, muted palette of green, gray and white exists in fine compositional balance.  The mottled, obscuring background, which actually includes the foreground swirling snow, works as pseudo-bokeh.  One of four personal favorites.', '2015-04-09 13:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340077, 1146662, 173844, '<td valign="top">A wonderful image.  The perfectly positioned and delineated legs get the show rolling.  The incredible shadow of the bird itself, cast on uneven ground,  shimmers in ragged, mirage-like fashion.  The bill alone is a revelation.  The interplay between a truncated reality and a coyly offered phantasmagoria shatters complacency, or at least the rut of "knowing".  The almost glaring backdrop to the shadow, consisting of water, sand or soil and upper legs, elicits a squint of presence.  I see in this image the unsteady birth of hieroglyphics.  One of four personal favorites.</td>', 'A wonderful image.  The perfectly positioned and delineated legs get the show rolling.  The incredible shadow of the bird itself, cast on uneven ground,  shimmers in ragged, mirage-like fashion.  The bill alone is a revelation.  The interplay between a truncated reality and a coyly offered phantasmagoria shatters complacency, or at least the rut of "knowing".  The almost glaring backdrop to the shadow, consisting of water, sand or soil and upper legs, elicits a squint of presence.  I see in this image the unsteady birth of hieroglyphics.  One of four personal favorites.', '2015-04-09 13:59:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340089, 1146636, 108069, '<td valign="top">It appears the weeds are trying to mimic this jawbone. Pretty interesting. A textural explosion.</td>', 'It appears the weeds are trying to mimic this jawbone. Pretty interesting. A textural explosion.', '2015-04-09 14:56:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340113, 1146298, 50695, '<td valign="top">I just finished a book about the history of science, and science pretty much begins with astronomy, because the heavenly bodies moved in orderly patterns, even though it took millennia to figure out what those patterns were. Surely some of those astronomers thought the sky was a blanket with holes in it...</td>', 'I just finished a book about the history of science, and science pretty much begins with astronomy, because the heavenly bodies moved in orderly patterns, even though it took millennia to figure out what those patterns were. Surely some of those astronomers thought the sky was a blanket with holes in it...', '2015-04-09 16:50:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340114, 1146652, 173844, '<td valign="top">What first leaps to mind when I see this image is the medium - it''s like a charcoal or soft pencil drawing on stippled paper.  Just beautiful before I''ve even taken in the content of the photo.  And the content is mysteriously, casually suggestive, be it sensual or workaday.  I think that this sort of hint of a wider, even explanatory, context is very fascinating to Ubique.  This image is a strong homage to him.  What in the world is up with that sawhorse?  The shapes, light and tones work on several levels to bring a strong, coherent composition to fruition.  Reminds me of pulp fiction covers of the 1930''s without being at all lurid.  One of four personal favorites.</td>', 'What first leaps to mind when I see this image is the medium - it''s like a charcoal or soft pencil drawing on stippled paper.  Just beautiful before I''ve even taken in the content of the photo.  And the content is mysteriously, casually suggestive, be it sensual or workaday.  I think that this sort of hint of a wider, even explanatory, context is very fascinating to Ubique.  This image is a strong homage to him.  What in the world is up with that sawhorse?  The shapes, light and tones work on several levels to bring a strong, coherent composition to fruition.  Reminds me of pulp fiction covers of the 1930''s without being at all lurid.  One of four personal favorites.', '2015-04-09 16:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340115, 1146634, 173844, '<td valign="top">This picture is --  and because it''s so casually overused I seldom use the word, but here goes  -- awesome.  First, it''s utterly straightforward, no added textures or tricky processing to concoct mood or heighten realism.  The marvelous shadows steal the show, plummeting predatory from the left, atwitter from the standbox and slipping away on the far right.  The composition is wonderful, weighted by the woman, a few inanimate objects, shadows and the lovely textured gray wall and sidewalk.  The bright yellow standbox echoed in her more muted yellow hat.  Her seeming obliviousness to the ephemeral drama.  I could go on and on, but already have...  One of four personal favorites in the challenge.</td>', 'This picture is --  and because it''s so casually overused I seldom use the word, but here goes  -- awesome.  First, it''s utterly straightforward, no added textures or tricky processing to concoct mood or heighten realism.  The marvelous shadows steal the show, plummeting predatory from the left, atwitter from the standbox and slipping away on the far right.  The composition is wonderful, weighted by the woman, a few inanimate objects, shadows and the lovely textured gray wall and sidewalk.  The bright yellow standbox echoed in her more muted yellow hat.  Her seeming obliviousness to the ephemeral drama.  I could go on and on, but already have...  One of four personal favorites in the challenge.', '2015-04-09 16:56:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340117, 1146473, 173844, '<td valign="top">A lovely, delicate, evocative image.  It''s a palimpsest from an ancient Sanskrit manuscript.  I can see the elephant and then hints of other animals in the bush.  A running person on the left, a pint of Ben &amp; Jerry''s in the center, but I guess part of the point is to unshackle the imagination.  The foliage looks like it''s been pressed between panes of glass.  I can almost hear a breathy flute in the background.  Beautiful and rewarding.  The title is great.</td>', 'A lovely, delicate, evocative image.  It''s a palimpsest from an ancient Sanskrit manuscript.  I can see the elephant and then hints of other animals in the bush.  A running person on the left, a pint of Ben & Jerry''s in the center, but I guess part of the point is to unshackle the imagination.  The foliage looks like it''s been pressed between panes of glass.  I can almost hear a breathy flute in the background.  Beautiful and rewarding.  The title is great.', '2015-04-09 17:12:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340118, 1146660, 50695, '<td valign="top">Niche photography... not meant to appeal to everyone. The bird has a niche and echoes the shape of the niche he is in. <br/> <br/>He lives in a sky full of niches.<br/> <br/>Beautiful textured photo, like a strip of wallpaper from Neverland... in other words the photo is itself an object.<br/> <br/>This is what eye candy should look like.</td>', 'Niche photography... not meant to appeal to everyone. The bird has a niche and echoes the shape of the niche he is in.  He lives in a sky full of niches. Beautiful textured photo, like a strip of wallpaper from Neverland... in other words the photo is itself an object. This is what eye candy should look like.', '2015-04-09 17:12:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340120, 1146054, 173844, '<td valign="top">A marvelous discovery that''s been treated to fine composition and processing.  If it sounds like I''m taking anything away from the photographer, I''m not at all.  This image is bursting with layers of mood, symbolism, irony and glee.  The title alone is worth the price of admission... if there were such.  Really enjoyable.</td>', 'A marvelous discovery that''s been treated to fine composition and processing.  If it sounds like I''m taking anything away from the photographer, I''m not at all.  This image is bursting with layers of mood, symbolism, irony and glee.  The title alone is worth the price of admission... if there were such.  Really enjoyable.', '2015-04-09 17:26:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340124, 1146708, 173844, '<td valign="top">I think this picture has something to do with sub-atomic particles flashing into and out of existence.  Alternatively, it''s Dr. Who''s wonder hound tracking renegade Daleks.  In any case, it''s provocatively fascinating and I certainly like it very much.  It''s the blown out void that''s central, framed by the front of the dog and the person''s legs and shoe.  It seems to say, "Don''t believe your eyes."</td>', 'I think this picture has something to do with sub-atomic particles flashing into and out of existence.  Alternatively, it''s Dr. Who''s wonder hound tracking renegade Daleks.  In any case, it''s provocatively fascinating and I certainly like it very much.  It''s the blown out void that''s central, framed by the front of the dog and the person''s legs and shoe.  It seems to say, "Don''t believe your eyes."', '2015-04-09 18:04:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340126, 1145865, 50695, '<td valign="top">this is a jarring crop, strangely close, as though we accidentally stumbled upon someone who is hiding.</td>', 'this is a jarring crop, strangely close, as though we accidentally stumbled upon someone who is hiding.', '2015-04-09 18:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340127, 1146484, 50695, '<td valign="top">a good example of photo-as-object and a sophisticated sort of eye candy, with complementary colors... and even a signature on the lower right, like a Japanese print.</td>', 'a good example of photo-as-object and a sophisticated sort of eye candy, with complementary colors... and even a signature on the lower right, like a Japanese print.', '2015-04-09 18:12:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7340130, 1146240, 50695, '<td valign="top">so much can be accomplished with a good crop. This photo is made disorienting and full of energetic swooping lines. Representation of reality takes second seat to the beauty of the composition.</td>', 'so much can be accomplished with a good crop. This photo is made disorienting and full of energetic swooping lines. Representation of reality takes second seat to the beauty of the composition.', '2015-04-09 18:13:14.000000', NULL, 1),
