(7341360, 1146711, 50695, '<td valign="top">so, the first two shots I''ve seen both have a striking thing in common: they create a strong sense of "false" drama. In other words, the reality of the situation is probably far less dramatic than what appears here. In this case, because of the expression you''ve caught on the girl''s face, and the way the foreground figures are lined up against her. Intriguing.</td>', 'so, the first two shots I''ve seen both have a striking thing in common: they create a strong sense of "false" drama. In other words, the reality of the situation is probably far less dramatic than what appears here. In this case, because of the expression you''ve caught on the girl''s face, and the way the foreground figures are lined up against her. Intriguing.', '2015-04-11 23:08:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341361, 1146710, 50695, '<td valign="top">Woman in Leather Jacket Standing Between Plastic Brides Mistaken For Mystical Goose By Man Receiving a Text That Says "Call Me Right Away"</td>', 'Woman in Leather Jacket Standing Between Plastic Brides Mistaken For Mystical Goose By Man Receiving a Text That Says "Call Me Right Away"', '2015-04-11 23:08:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341363, 1146598, 50695, '<td valign="top">I love windshields as filters. It''s the romance of the road, and also the sad isolation of the wanderer. The windshield is the lens and the car is the camera, taking one big picture of a country, capturing so much and losing so much. Yes, I drove by you and I saw you. No, I don''t know what you were thinking or feeling, but you were near the road that I was on, so that road connects us... you know... like a bridge... or a bird flying to find a sanctuary and bring you back a piece of it.</td>', 'I love windshields as filters. It''s the romance of the road, and also the sad isolation of the wanderer. The windshield is the lens and the car is the camera, taking one big picture of a country, capturing so much and losing so much. Yes, I drove by you and I saw you. No, I don''t know what you were thinking or feeling, but you were near the road that I was on, so that road connects us... you know... like a bridge... or a bird flying to find a sanctuary and bring you back a piece of it.', '2015-04-11 23:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341364, 1146652, 50695, '<td valign="top">Everybody has feet. It''s what holds us up. Even the floor has feet. You know because you see the steps.</td>', 'Everybody has feet. It''s what holds us up. Even the floor has feet. You know because you see the steps.', '2015-04-11 23:08:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341365, 1146354, 50695, '<td valign="top">the small size and blur gives the person a menacing mane, and of course the glowing eyes of the beast. The viewer is the pursued, trapped in a narrow alley (much as cameras trap reality into a small frame).<br/> <br/>And the pursuers, well, they''re in no hurry. They know they''ve won.</td>', 'the small size and blur gives the person a menacing mane, and of course the glowing eyes of the beast. The viewer is the pursued, trapped in a narrow alley (much as cameras trap reality into a small frame). And the pursuers, well, they''re in no hurry. They know they''ve won.', '2015-04-11 23:09:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341366, 1146463, 50695, '<td valign="top">that water seems unreal, or more real than the photo, as if you''re getting my computer wet.</td>', 'that water seems unreal, or more real than the photo, as if you''re getting my computer wet.', '2015-04-11 23:09:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341368, 1146135, 50695, '<td valign="top">I know this is a religious order, but it''s difficult not to find such masked hoods menacing. The stoic face peering at us actually feels like a comfort, convincing us that nothing dangerous is happening. In fact, to him, the photographer is more interesting than the parade. I find this tension between event and bored viewer of event keeps me looking between the two, and thus creates an energy in the divided image. It also suggests to me that the man and the photographer and the viewer are in their own parade, just as masked and mysterious.<br/> <br/>wait a minute... I think I just saw a pony...</td>', 'I know this is a religious order, but it''s difficult not to find such masked hoods menacing. The stoic face peering at us actually feels like a comfort, convincing us that nothing dangerous is happening. In fact, to him, the photographer is more interesting than the parade. I find this tension between event and bored viewer of event keeps me looking between the two, and thus creates an energy in the divided image. It also suggests to me that the man and the photographer and the viewer are in their own parade, just as masked and mysterious. wait a minute... I think I just saw a pony...', '2015-04-11 23:09:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341369, 1146435, 50695, '<td valign="top">The foreground waitress is beautiful, and painted by a Sumi-e brush. The diners are absorbed into the wall mural. These are subtle but very strange effects, making this photo not like other photos. It''s not a photo *of* something interesting or important. It''s a record of an unusual point of view, a hint at seeing the world in a different way.</td>', 'The foreground waitress is beautiful, and painted by a Sumi-e brush. The diners are absorbed into the wall mural. These are subtle but very strange effects, making this photo not like other photos. It''s not a photo *of* something interesting or important. It''s a record of an unusual point of view, a hint at seeing the world in a different way.', '2015-04-11 23:10:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341370, 1146371, 50695, '<td valign="top">I know that girl. By drawing on a window, she combines her artwork with the world outside (or the world inside depending on where you''re standing). By photographing her, you capture the process of these worlds combining, and you capture the artist, and the strong shadows on her face are similar to the dark shapes in her artwork, so you suggest that the whole thing is one artwork.<br/> <br/>Or I could just go with Feminist Theory and say this is another old white guy stealing a woman''s art.... ;)</td>', 'I know that girl. By drawing on a window, she combines her artwork with the world outside (or the world inside depending on where you''re standing). By photographing her, you capture the process of these worlds combining, and you capture the artist, and the strong shadows on her face are similar to the dark shapes in her artwork, so you suggest that the whole thing is one artwork. Or I could just go with Feminist Theory and say this is another old white guy stealing a woman''s art.... ;)', '2015-04-11 23:10:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341372, 1146054, 50695, '<td valign="top">I admire this because it''s hard to pull off. the layers of the signs, and being cut across by wires, the unpropitious elements all work together to create something new.</td>', 'I admire this because it''s hard to pull off. the layers of the signs, and being cut across by wires, the unpropitious elements all work together to create something new.', '2015-04-11 23:11:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341382, 1146105, 50695, '<td valign="top">this photo is almost too successful. It almost solves itself. The people in the background are perfect foils for the beautiful protagonist, who seems about to confront them. I almost forget that I have no idea what is actually going on. This could easily be a still from a movie (in square format). Yes, that''s it. It''s like a grainy Cindy Sherman photo, but I don''t think it''s set up. But it could be.<br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'this photo is almost too successful. It almost solves itself. The people in the background are perfect foils for the beautiful protagonist, who seems about to confront them. I almost forget that I have no idea what is actually going on. This could easily be a still from a movie (in square format). Yes, that''s it. It''s like a grainy Cindy Sherman photo, but I don''t think it''s set up. But it could be. I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341383, 1146662, 50695, '<td valign="top">just the right amount of blur and noise and cropping to achieve ... unity between reality and dream. This is not done, as some think, merely by making a mess. It actually requires a careful balance. Showing too much shadow and reflection ruins the effect. It''s like lucid dreaming... you know you''re in the dream, so you''re not worried. This photo keeps you in the dream and doesn''t let you know it''s a dream.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'just the right amount of blur and noise and cropping to achieve ... unity between reality and dream. This is not done, as some think, merely by making a mess. It actually requires a careful balance. Showing too much shadow and reflection ruins the effect. It''s like lucid dreaming... you know you''re in the dream, so you''re not worried. This photo keeps you in the dream and doesn''t let you know it''s a dream.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341384, 1145714, 50695, '<td valign="top">There is of course a barrier between the viewer and whatever it is that the viewer sees in the photo.<br/> <br/>You could call that barrier a door.<br/> <br/>You could call that barrier two doors. She threatens to close the first door. The second door... why, that''s near enough for us to grab it, to prevent her from closing it, or to close it ourselves, or to pull it open further.<br/> <br/>It took me some effort to write this out, but I am merely describing the very first thing I felt when I saw the image... the physics of two doors belonging to the same body. and every part of this image contributes to that effect. I know you''re not Michelangelo laboring over every square inch of your canvas, you''re just a lucky so-and-so who knows which photos are lucky... but really you and Michelangelo are the same, the gods of imagery are smiling upon you.<br/> <br/>Posthumous Blue Ribbon<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077284" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077284.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077284.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077284.jpg"/></a></td>', 'There is of course a barrier between the viewer and whatever it is that the viewer sees in the photo. You could call that barrier a door. You could call that barrier two doors. She threatens to close the first door. The second door... why, that''s near enough for us to grab it, to prevent her from closing it, or to close it ourselves, or to pull it open further. It took me some effort to write this out, but I am merely describing the very first thing I felt when I saw the image... the physics of two doors belonging to the same body. and every part of this image contributes to that effect. I know you''re not Michelangelo laboring over every square inch of your canvas, you''re just a lucky so-and-so who knows which photos are lucky... but really you and Michelangelo are the same, the gods of imagery are smiling upon you. Posthumous Blue Ribbon ', '2015-04-11 23:15:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341385, 1146564, 50695, '<td valign="top">I think this is the wrong side of the mirror, but it works anyway. Well it mostly works, except it made the dog sideways. Well, dog star, actually, but it fell out of the sky because it''s daytime and because the mirror is backwards.<br/> <br/>Some things just can''t be done with Instagram. We still need photographers. Thank you.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I think this is the wrong side of the mirror, but it works anyway. Well it mostly works, except it made the dog sideways. Well, dog star, actually, but it fell out of the sky because it''s daytime and because the mirror is backwards. Some things just can''t be done with Instagram. We still need photographers. Thank you.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341386, 1146436, 50695, '<td valign="top">this is the worst possible angle for a boring photograph. any chance of this photo being ordinary has been ruined. I hope you''re happy.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'this is the worst possible angle for a boring photograph. any chance of this photo being ordinary has been ruined. I hope you''re happy.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341387, 1146534, 50695, '<td valign="top">strange image breaking the rules. an exciting arrangement of whites.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'strange image breaking the rules. an exciting arrangement of whites.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341388, 1146577, 50695, '<td valign="top">this photo has some life in it. The bird against the sky, of course, but also the way the bird is made part of the horizon, and is accompanied by other odd shapes, which we eventually realize is a dramatic landscape that you''ve robbed of drama, and replaced with a sense of quotidian randomness. the angle and composition with so much sky serve to emphasize the unimportance of what''s on the ground. The line held up by no parking signs is broken. A pickup truck is parked, mocking the sentinel. Like all good humor, this has some tragedy in it. This is the sorrow and hilarity of how trivial our concerns are.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'this photo has some life in it. The bird against the sky, of course, but also the way the bird is made part of the horizon, and is accompanied by other odd shapes, which we eventually realize is a dramatic landscape that you''ve robbed of drama, and replaced with a sense of quotidian randomness. the angle and composition with so much sky serve to emphasize the unimportance of what''s on the ground. The line held up by no parking signs is broken. A pickup truck is parked, mocking the sentinel. Like all good humor, this has some tragedy in it. This is the sorrow and hilarity of how trivial our concerns are.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341389, 1146460, 50695, '<td valign="top">some photos look back at you. There''s something to be said for this. It''s like a car that has to turn once in a while or it will never get back home.<br/> <br/>This look, back at us, eradicates other things the photo might be, like a study of textures. All of that is twisted into a backward look. The artistic experience is one of confrontation. The boy owns this photo as much as the viewer does.<br/> <br/>It''s a matter of degree. What can you do to moderate that powerful look? You make it small. You keep it in the center but you make it small, and you twist it away from the direction of everything else in the photo. Now the photo is active and alive and not some dead portrait of a stranger.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'some photos look back at you. There''s something to be said for this. It''s like a car that has to turn once in a while or it will never get back home. This look, back at us, eradicates other things the photo might be, like a study of textures. All of that is twisted into a backward look. The artistic experience is one of confrontation. The boy owns this photo as much as the viewer does. It''s a matter of degree. What can you do to moderate that powerful look? You make it small. You keep it in the center but you make it small, and you twist it away from the direction of everything else in the photo. Now the photo is active and alive and not some dead portrait of a stranger.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7341390, 1146634, 50695, '<td valign="top">the secret of this photo is scale. the shadows seem impossibly big, and the woman seems overwhelmed but indifferent.<br/> <br/> <br/>I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'the secret of this photo is scale. the shadows seem impossibly big, and the woman seems overwhelmed but indifferent.  I''m hanging this in my fantasy gallery ', '2015-04-11 23:15:56.000000', NULL, 1),
